        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-23T09:43:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem very robust and we really don\u0027t want to have false negatives in a check like this (as that would compromise the privacy/security of the pVM). \n\nProbably dumb question but why don\u0027t we simply return `!result.getStdout().empty()`? Is it because `stdout` contains many other logs (from crosvm, UART, ...)? If so, is there a kernel tag we could instead grep for?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 219,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 219,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "c03f66171425c0aec268615f59f4705bac0e50f4",
